Valkyries seem to be one of the more popular "easy" characters to
ascend, but I've never had much luck with them myself. I've won
offline with a human Valk before in a previous version, so I decided
to try a dwarf this time. My first few attempts ended in failure,
sadly as if I'd been able to ascend my first NAO Valk I would have
extended my ascension streak to three. Was not to be, but fourth time
was the charm.

A magic lamp and bones pile in the Mines helped me get started out
right with silver dragon scale and cloak of magic resistance, and soon
a bag of holding as well so I could skip Sokoban (which I hate)
altogether. I was nervous about not having poison resistance, but
ended up getting crowned quite early, which took care of everything
except disintegration (acquired much later). Polytrap helped turn my
starting pet cat Pepper into a yellow dragon, which proved amazingly
useful; stoning-resistant, she happily killed and ate cockatrices for
me (I don't like carrying rubber chickens around, so usually just tin
them to keep them out of the hands of intelligent monsters). I also
found a saddle and had fun riding a bit, though never got beyond the
unskilled level.

I dipped for Excalibur and used that until I got the requisite
Mjollnir. Quest was tricky as I had no means of levitation, and no way
to fireproof my water walking boots for the lava levels. I ended up
freezing the lava to walk over it, but eventually took a misstep and
dissolved my boots. Here's where riding my pet dragon came in handy!
We flew over and killed the quest enemy, then flew all the way back to
the main dungeon. I replaced the ww boots later, but never did find
boots or ring of levitation, nor any wands of polymorph to try to
generate some (my one polymorphed item was a result of dipping to ID a
potion); ended up wishing for the lev boots at the Castle on the way
back up.

Black dragon eventually disintegrated poor Pepper; too bad, I thought
it would have been fun to try to ascend with my starting (albeit
polymorphed) pet. At some point I acquired two more pets, an Angel and
an Aleax, and tried to get them to wield Sunsword and Excalibur,
respectively (I was dual-weaponing Frost Brand with a silver saber by
this time, with Mjollnir as a backup for ranged attacks once I finally
wished up some gauntlets of power). I couldn't seem to convince them
to drop their long swords in favor of the artifact weapons. Finally I
searched this newsgroup and found the solution; applying a bullwhip, I
yanked the inferior weapons out of their grasp, and they then picked
up and wielded the artifacts. The Aleax fell prey to another
disintegration blast (very annoying, but I was going for no-genocide)
on the way out of Gehennom, but I kept the Angel all the way up to the
Plane of Fire, where despite healing her damage, she declined to
follow me to the next Plane.

No-genocide conduct made dealing with liches, flayers, and sea
monsters annoying. I did manage to only get mind-flayed once, and even
that time probably would have been avoidable with better use of my
teleport wand. Liches I just had to beat to the upstair and beat up. I
wasn't risking losing Mjollnir in water to throw it at eels, so I
tried force bolt spell (took a long time to get smart enough to cast
anything; potions of gain ability were nearly absent, and pet dragon
ate most of the mind flayer corpses), wands of cold, etc., and
teleported some onto dry land for easy kills.

Rodney wasn't too annoying, Planes were OK with Orb of Fate to help
locate the portals, never had to deal with Pestilence, and on the
second high altar I offered and ascended. That makes five NAO
ascensions; four classes (PTHV) and three races (@Gh) so far. Not sure
what I'll try next; I really missed spellcasting in this game, so
possibly a Wizard.

